Summary: file_editor: {"command": "create", "file_text": "# REPORT: Sorting Algorithm Benchmark\n\n## Research 
Question\nHow do input size and input order affect the running time of insertion sort, merge sort, and Python's built-in
sorted()?\n\n## Methodology\n\n### Algorithms Tested\n1. **insertion_sort** \u2014 Pure Python, in-place insertion sort.
Theoretical: O(n\u00b2) worst/average, O(n) best.\n2. **merge_sort** \u2014 Pure Python, top-down recursive merge sort 
with auxiliary merge. Theoretical: O(n log n) in all cases.\n3. **sorted** \u2014 Python's built-in `sorted()`, which 
uses Timsort (a hybrid of merge sort and insertion sort), implemented in C.\n\n### Correctness Verification\nAll three 
algorithms were tested against Python's `sorted()` on 11 test cases:\n- empty list, single element, two elements, two 
equal elements\n- duplicates, negatives, mixed negative/positive\n- already sorted, reverse sorted, all same elements\n-
large random (2000 elements with duplicates)\n\n**Result: All 33 tests (3 algorithms \u00d7 11 cases) PASSED.**\n\n### 
Benchmark Design\n- **Input sizes**: 100, 1000, 3000\n- **Input types**: random, sorted (ascending), reverse-sorted 
(descending)\n- **Random seeds**: 5 fixed seeds (42, 123, 456, 789, 1000)\n- **Repetitions**: 50 per configuration\n- 
**Warm-up**: 10 runs before timing begins\n- **Timing**: `time.perf_counter_ns()` for nanosecond precision\n- **Input 
sharing**: Each algorithm receives an identical copy of the same generated input data\n- **Total measurements**: 3 sizes
\u00d7 3 input types \u00d7 5 seeds \u00d7 3 algorithms \u00d7 50 repetitions = **6,750 individual measurements**\n\n###
Data Collection\nAll individual measurements saved to `results.csv` with columns:\n`algorithm, size, input_type, seed, 
repetition, elapsed_ns, correct`\n\n### Reproduction\n```bash\ncd /workspace\npython3 algorithms.py\n```\n\n## Measured 
Results\n\n### Mean Elapsed Time (nanoseconds)\n\n| Algorithm        | Size | Input Type     | Mean (ns)    | Std Dev 
(ns) |\n|------------------|------|----------------|--------------|--------------|\n| insertion_sort   | 100  | random  
